# Git sync with GitHub

This project lives at [QimingTian/Heroes-Around-Me-Website](https://github.com/QimingTian/Heroes-Around-Me-Website).

- **Remote**: `origin` → `https://github.com/QimingTian/Heroes-Around-Me-Website.git`
- **Branch**: `main` (local should track `origin/main`)

## Keep local and GitHub in sync

**Before making changes** (or when starting a session on this project):

```bash
git fetch origin
git pull origin main
```

**After completing requested changes** (when the user wants work saved or published):

1. `git status` — commit all relevant site files (HTML, CSS, JS, images).
2. One clear commit message per logical change (or one commit if the user asks for a single push).
3. `git push origin main`

**If push is rejected** (remote has new commits): `git pull --rebase origin main`, then push again. Do not force-push `main` unless the user explicitly asks.

## Vercel deployment

- **Production URL**: https://heroes-around-me-website.vercel.app
- **Project**: `heroes-around-me-website` on Vercel (GitHub repo connected — pushes to `main` trigger production deploys).
- **Manual deploy** (if needed): `vercel deploy --prod` from the project root (requires Vercel CLI login).

Do not change `git config`. The user is signed into GitHub on this machine.
